                "retweet_count": 455,
                "source": "Sprout Social",
                "text": "You might think that if you don\u2019t get health insurance through the ACA marketplace, Republicans letting the tax credits expire won\u2019t impact you. But it will.\n\nWhen insurance costs skyrocket, more people\u2014especially younger, healthier folks\u2014are going to drop their coverage completely. When that happens, insurers charge everyone else more.\n\nMore uninsured people means more people will show up at emergency rooms unable to pay. Hospitals will be forced to charge everyone else to make up for those loses.\n\nAnd for some smaller hospitals and rural clinics, fewer people with health insurance means fewer people coming through the doors, forcing them to close entirely and leaving fewer options for people in the area.\n\nWhether you get health insurance through your work or the ACA marketplace, everyone\u2019s health care costs are going to rise because of President Trump.",
